# Maltese translation for xdg-user-dirs — A PROPOSAL, NOT SUBMITTED.
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS UPSTREAM AS IT IS.
#
# Status: NEEDS REVIEW BY A MALTESE SPEAKER. Every msgstr below was written
# by an alo OS contributor who is not one, on 2026-10-28, from general
# knowledge of Maltese computing vocabulary. Nobody who reads Maltese has
# checked a single line. Submitting it is the owner's decision, made
# separately, and only after that review.
#
# Why it exists: xdg-user-dirs, which every Linux desktop names a person's
# home folders with, ships no Maltese catalogue (measured 2026-10-28 in
# Fedora 42's xdg-user-dirs 0.18: 22 of the 24 official EU languages are
# there, English is the source, Maltese is the one missing). So a Maltese
# person's folders are named in English on every Linux desktop, alo OS's
# included (ADR 0137). The remedy is a translation in xdg-user-dirs itself,
# where every desktop gets it, not a list of alo OS's own.
#
# What a reviewer is asked:
#   - Is each name the ordinary word a Maltese speaker expects for this folder
#     on a computer (the one Windows and macOS use in Maltese, if they do)?
#   - Is a name better left in English where Maltese usage keeps English
#     (msgstr "" leaves the English name)?
#   - Each name becomes a real folder: no slash, no leading dot.
#
# The eight msgids are xdg-user-dirs' own, from /etc/xdg/user-dirs.defaults.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: xdg-user-dirs\n"
"Language: mt\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=4; plural=(n==1 ? 0 : n==0 || ( n%100>1 && n%100<11) ? 1 : (n%100>10 && n%100<20 ) ? 2 : 3);\n"

# Unsure: Maltese computing usage commonly keeps "Desktop".
msgid "Desktop"
msgstr "Desktop"

msgid "Documents"
msgstr "Dokumenti"

# Unsure: "Tniżżil" is the noun for a download; usage may keep "Downloads".
msgid "Downloads"
msgstr "Tniżżil"

msgid "Music"
msgstr "Mużika"

msgid "Pictures"
msgstr "Stampi"

msgid "Public"
msgstr "Pubbliku"

# Unsure: "Mudelli" (models, patterns) is offered for document templates.
msgid "Templates"
msgstr "Mudelli"

# Unsure: "Vidjows" is a loan; "Filmati" is also used.
msgid "Videos"
msgstr "Vidjows"
